      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are some extreme versions of the frugality and influence jokes:\n\nFrugality:\n\n* \"I'm not cheap, I'm just passionately invested in the value of a dollar. I once spent 20 minutes debating the price of a sandwich with the guy behind the counter.\"\n* \"My grandma was a hoarder, but I'm more like her in that I hoard pennies. I have a jar at home that's like a tiny, sad bank vault.\"\n* \"I'm not stingy, I'm just... calculating. Like, have you seen the interest rates on a good credit card? It's like they're trying to rob me blind.\"\n\nInfluence:\n\n* \"I know a guy who knows a guy who can get you a table at the hottest restaurant in town... for a 20% commission. It's like a timeshare, but with better food.\"\n* \"I'm not 'well-connected,' I'm just... familiar with the right people. Like, I know the guy who delivers the pastrami sandwiches at the deli. He's like a friend, but with more meat.\"\n* \"I've got a 'network' of friends who owe me favors. Like, my cousin's brother",
